  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Thermal and humidity control of the crewed cabin: condensing heat exchangers remove metabolic heat (≈100 W per crew member) and condensate from cabin air, maintaining 18-27°C and 25-75% relative humidity. Liquid-cooling garments, cabin air coolers, and coolant loops interface with the spacecraft's external thermal control subsystem to reject waste heat to space via radiators.",
  "early_win": false,
